      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "type": "nodetool.workflows.base_node.Comment",
        "data": {
          "comment": "# Lip-sync a Clip to a Voice Track\n\nSyncs your presenter clip to a voice track you already have. Use it to re-voice footage without reshooting.\n\n**How it works:** \"Voice track\" passes through \"Even out volume\" (Normalize), then \"Soften the start\" with a 0.01 second fade-in and \"Soften the ending\" with a 0.03 second fade-out. \"Lip-sync to the voice track\" matches the mouth movement in \"Presenter clip\" to that audio with fal sync-lipsync v2 pro, and \"Re-voiced clip\" shows the result. The audio steps run locally. Lip-sync is a paid step billed per second of footage.\n\n**Try this:** Set \"duration\" on \"Soften the ending\" to 0.3. The voice fades out more gently at the end of the clip."
        },
